1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,167
Saturday afternoon. A bench in the culture-center lobby.

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:07,500
There he goes again. His kid's award photo! Is this chat a bragging contest?!

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,200
Moragu, don't be like that. Humility is best.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,933
Dad, you posted my jump-rope certificate earlier.

5
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:16,800
That was just a keepsake. So what~

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:21,633
Sir. I saw you write, 'Omg, my kid won again.'

7
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:26,667
Theirs: a bragging contest. Mine: a keepsake. Double standard, number one.

8
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:29,067
I'm… Modapman.

9
00:00:29,067 --> 00:00:33,367
If I do it, so what. If you do it: rude! The kid-bragging edition.

10
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,200
Round one: holiday questions.

11
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,333
My uncle always asks, 'What rank did you get?' Nosy! Just nosy!

12
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:41,267
And that afternoon, at the cousins' gathering.

13
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:45,633
So, what rank this year? I ask because I worry~ So what~

14
00:00:45,633 --> 00:00:48,800
Dad, that cousin looks like he doesn't want to answer.

15
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:53,700
They pry: nosy. I ask: concern. Double standard, number two.

16
00:00:53,700 --> 00:01:00,667
Sir, one study. We tend to blame circumstances for our own acts, and character for other people's.

17
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:02,933
You only see your own reasons!

18
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:05,533
Round two: the humble brag.

19
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:09,800
Look at her. 'My kid does well without studying.' That's bragging, plain and simple!

20
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:15,533
It's nothing, but… I'm worried Moragu's certificates will make his room too small, crying.

21
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:16,667
Translation: bragging.

22
00:01:16,667 --> 00:01:22,733
Their humility: a disguised brag. My worry: real worry. Double standard, number three.

23
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:30,733
In studies, bragging disguised as worry or modesty scored lower on likability and competence than plain bragging. It's called a humblebrag.

24
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:32,867
…Should've just bragged?

25
00:01:32,867 --> 00:01:34,767
Dad, you could just not.

26
00:01:34,767 --> 00:01:36,500
Round three: tutoring tips.

27
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:40,400
That mom 'shares tips' but she's really advertising her kid's academy!

28
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:45,233
Sharing the English academy we go to, for your benefit~ Top-level class, by the way~

29
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:46,367
Translation: bragging.

30
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:50,333
Their tips: advertising. My tips: charity. Double standard, number four.

31
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:54,600
When we see other parents brag, we start comparing our kid. It's called social comparison.

32
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:57,000
So that's why your heart wobbles.

33
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,867
Right. Theirs, and yours.

34
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:02,267
Bonus round. Rapid-fire double standards!

35
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:06,400
Praise for their kid: flattery. Praise for mine: objective assessment!

36
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:10,367
Their first-birthday party: showing off. Mine: once in a lifetime!

37
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:14,167
They post kid photos: advertising. Me: a memory log!

38
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:17,967
They say 'my kid is sweet': cringe. Me: fact!

39
00:02:17,967 --> 00:02:22,600
Double standard: five, six, seven, eight!

40
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,167
Dad, I felt good that you posted my certificate.

41
00:02:25,167 --> 00:02:27,833
But some friends might feel bad.

42
00:02:27,833 --> 00:02:28,100
…Yeah.

43
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:32,133
You want to brag because you're happy. Then tell me directly.

44
00:02:32,133 --> 00:02:36,967
…Moragu, you jump rope so well. Dad almost cried.

45
00:02:36,967 --> 00:02:40,233
Share good news with those closest to you first. That's the best way.

46
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:42,700
That night, the parents' group chat.

47
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:46,400
Dad, uploading ten photos at once.

48
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:52,800
It's nothing, but Moragu won an award at the jump-rope contest hehe. Worried about room space.

49
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:57,200
Oh yes hehe, mine got one too. Every participant did~

50
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,200
Dad, they give it to every participant.

51
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:02,133
…Still, it's a keepsake. So what.

52
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:04,200
Honey. The room isn't small.

53
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:09,700
Others: bragging. Me: a keepsake. Double standard, nine and ten.

54
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:10,600
Just a wrong answer.

55
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:13,000
…Classic Modapman.
